  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Opportunity for scattered afternoon/evening \nshowers/storms beginning Thursday and continuing through early \nnext week.\n\nExpect development of river valley fog in the mountain valleys \nagain tonight otherwise remaining mostly clear and dry until\nreturn of deeper moisture Thursday afternoon.\n\nThe upper ridge of high pressure over the TN valley is forecast\nto weaken and retrograde farther west and become centered over \nthe Ark-La-Tex by the weekend. This will allow a front over the\nGreat Lakes to sag south over the Mid-Atlantic with increasing \nmoisture leading to a daily chance for showers and a few storms \nbeginning Thursday and persisting through early next week. \nOverall, severe threat remains low given lack of shear to \nsupport organized deep convection. \n\nWarmest temperatures will occur Thursday and Friday, featuring\nwidespread upper 80s to mid 90s. Will see temperatures lower \nsomewhat again over the weekend and early next week as the \nridging shifts west, but will still be above normal for mid\nSeptember.",
